  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily and Dad go to a toy shop. It is Tom's birthday today. The sign on the door says: \"Toy shop.\" Another sign says: \"Open.\" \"What does Tom like?\" asks Dad. \"Tom likes horses,\" says Lily. She sees a big sign with an arrow. It says: \"Animal toys. This way.\"",
      "They go to the animal toys. Lily sees a small brown horse. She sees a white goat. She sees a big gray hippo. \"The hippo is funny,\" says Lily. \"But Tom likes the horse.\" \"Is this the horse?\" asks Dad. \"Yes, it is,\" says Lily. \"It is a good birthday toy!\"",
      "Next to the horses, there is a sign. It says: \"Ship toys.\" Lily sees a big blue ship. \"Tom likes ships too,\" she says. Dad gets the horse. Then they go to the door. A sign on the door says: \"Goodbye!\" \"Goodbye!\" says Lily. Tom is happy at home."
    ],
    "summary": "Lily and Dad go to a toy shop for Tom's birthday. They read the signs and find a toy horse.",
